d to this level."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level."}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn5le04ob04re1img01.png"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "J and Y Sounds"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "The English letters J and Y have different sounds.  They can be difficult to pronounce because the sound is similar."}, {"type": "text", "content": "To pronounce the y sound, the mid/front part of the tongue raises and presses against the roof of the mouth. The tip of the tongue comes down and lightly touches behind the bottom front teeth."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Say the words:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "yellow, yes, yoke, youth"}, {"type": "text", "content": "To pronounce the j sound, close your teeth and move your tongue up to cut off the flow of air. Say something while quickly lowering your tongue and opening your teeth slightly."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Say the words:  "}, {"type": "text", "content": "jello, joke, jester "}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "eatery "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a small and informal restaurant "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The food is usually great at the Bayside Eatery."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le04ob04aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you hear in a conversation about a city."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "yolk "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the yellow part in the center of an egg "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: My eggs looked more grey than yellow. It must be the yolks."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le04ob04aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "fog "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "many small drops of water floating in the air making it hard to see "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: There is a lot of fog in the summer in San Francisco."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le04ob04aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "sprint  "}, {"type": "definition", "content": " to run or go very fast for a short distance "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Get ready for a ten mile sprint!"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le04ob04aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "joker  "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a person who tells or makes many jokes  "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I was always the joker of the group."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le04ob04aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "trail"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a path through a forest or field "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: We can jog along the bay trail tomorrow."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le04ob04aud06"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to head up "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to go upwards along a path, mountain, or trail "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": " (verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: We head up the mountain this afternoon."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le04ob04aud07"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "out the window  "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "gone or wasted "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: My routine is out the window."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le04ob04aud08"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "bloated  "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "very swollen; too full of food or liquid   "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I feel bloated after that meal."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le04ob04aud09"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "current  "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "movement of water or air in the same direction "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The ocean currents can affect the weather."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le04ob04aud10"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Say these minimal pairs aloud with a partner."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Choose 8 words from the table. (4 <span class=\"italic\">Y</span> words and 4 <span class=\"italic\">J</span> words)"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write 4 sentences.  Each sentence must contain 1 word starting with <span class=\"italic\">Y</span> and <span class=\"italic\">J</span>."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Read the sentences aloud to a partner."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":11,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Y</span> sound\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">J</span> sound\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"yam \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"jam\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"yard\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"jarred\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"yet \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"jet\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"c